description.narrative:
The project seeks to bolster UNESCO’s Global Education Coalition's Latin America and the Caribbean chapter by fostering the advancement of quality distance education and training throughout the region. Specifically, it will provide targeted assistance to Ecuador, enhancing its ability to introduce top-tier distance and blended learning initiatives into its education systems, thus propelling the digital transformation of education forward.

The project will undertake the following interventions:

•	Enhancing digital skills and proficiency in blended learning methodologies among teacher trainers, teachers, and education leaders;
•	Strengthening 21st century skills among teachers, trainers and education leaders; 
•	Building the capacity of teachers, trainers, and education leaders to implement gender transformative pedagogies and education in crisis contexts;
•	Develop skills to mainstream emerging issues in education such as artificial intelligence, education for sustainable development, and citizenship education.
•	Facilitating heightened motivation and access to collaborative professional development networks, such as Communities of Practice, for educators across Ecuador.
